      "standardized_narrative": "During 2023 the syndicate strengthened reserves materially, driven primarily by significant uncertainty and adverse development relating to Russian/Ukraine aviation exposures (notably western-leased aircraft in Russia) and prior-year deterioration within the Casualty business due to construction defect litigation in Florida and emerging UK cladding-related PI exposures. Inflation and higher claims costs were also considered in setting best estimate reserves. Overall, gross claims outstanding increased materially year-on-year, with the syndicate applying probabilistic scenario modelling for the Russia/Ukraine exposures and booking additional IBNR for casualty and professional indemnity risks.",
